{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.selfDual_iff_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.selfDual_iff_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.lean#L47-L49","doc":"The self-dual shells are exactly the fixed points of the transpose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.SelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.SelfDual","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.lean#L43-L45","doc":"A partition indexes a self-dual shell iff it is self-conjugate\n(`λ = λ*`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.conj_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.conj_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.lean#L38-L41","doc":"Hence the transpose is a bijection of the index set — `GLₖ`-duality\npermutes the Schur–Weyl indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.conj_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.conj_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.lean#L35-L36","doc":"The transpose is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.conj_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.conj_conj","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Transpose is involutive: `(λ*)* = λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.conj","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.lean#L27-L27","doc":"The transpose / conjugate partition `λ ↦ λ*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.Partition","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.lean#L25-L25","doc":"The partition index set (partitions `λ ⊢ n`, `≤ k` rows). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.lean#L23-L23","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality","kind":"structure","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality.lean#L18-L29","doc":"Data for shell Schur–Weyl self-duality.\n\nA `definition` carrier: the index set of partitions `λ ⊢ n` and the\nconjugation (transpose) `conj = (·)*`, with the involutivity that makes it\na duality. ","signatureChunk":0}]}